They come from QEMU's existing
TPM Physical Presence Interface implementation and from the UTM/QEMU SysBus
TPM series that makes those pieces usable with dynamically allocated Arm
platform-bus MMIO addresses.

* Upstream QEMU PPI ACPI/shared-memory implementation:
  * ac6dd31e3fe7 ("acpi: build TPM Physical Presence interface")
  * 3b97c01e9ccd ("tpm: allocate/map buffer for TPM Physical Presence
    interface")
* UTM/QEMU ARM SysBus TPM backport source series:
  * c1bd61b8ec50 ("tpm_ppi: refactor memory space initialization")
    splits PPI RAM initialization from address-space mapping so a SysBus TPM
    device can expose the PPI region through the platform bus instead of the
    fixed x86 ``TPM_PPI_ADDR_BASE`` mapping.
  * 3f0d5bac18fb ("tpm_tis_sysbus: move DSDT AML generation to device")
    moves SysBus TPM AML generation into the device model so the device can
    report the platform-bus-assigned MMIO address to ACPI.
  * 4653477a126a ("tpm_crb_sysbus: introduce TPM CRB SysBus device")
    introduces ``tpm-crb-device`` for Arm ``virt`` and documents why this CRB
    SysBus path is the one UTM uses for Windows 11 ARM64, while
    ``tpm-tis-device`` is not sufficient for current Windows drivers.

